r and have not been reviewed by the authors.","citation_ids":["cite.euler.theorem-a.1"],"evidence_ids":["link.euler.theorem-a.1"],"id":"euler.theorem-a.1","kind":"claim","label":"Theorem A.1","locator":"Theorem A.1, Section A","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Theorem A.1.** Under (A.1)–(A.2), let $L\\in C(I;C^{0,1/2})$. There are unique $z\\in C^1(I;C^{0,1/2})$, $c\\in C^{0,1/2}$ divergence free and $\\nabla\\phi\\in C(I;C^{0,1/2})$ satisfying $$Kz_t-J(\\Omega z_t)+L=c+\\nabla\\phi,\n \\qquad \\operatorname{div}z=0,\\qquad z(0)=z(1)=0.$$ They obey $$\\begin{equation}\n \\left\\lVert z_t\\right\\rVert_0\\le CQ^p\\left\\lVert L\\right\\rVert_0. \\tag{A.3}\n\\end{equation}$$ If $K$, $\\Omega$ and $L$ are smooth on $I\\times\\mathbb T^3$, then so are $z$, $c$ and $\\nabla\\phi$.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.theorem-a.1","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.theorem-4.2","id":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.theorem-4.2%22%2C%22euler.theorem-a.1%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.theorem-4.2%22%2C%22euler.theorem-a.1%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.theorem-a.1"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.theorem-a.1","id":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.theorem-a.1%22%2C%22euler.lemma-a.2%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.theorem-a.1%22%2C